  "status_text": "The question behind the 04:42 note has a first answer from one of our own seats, on smaller graphs (computed, not checked): cheapest circuits with the stray part in them do exist, on two five-vertex graphs with a triangle, so that narrow hope is gone there. But in each of the 14 such circuits found a different inclusion survives, and it is the one the three-gate step really needs: the step still closes on all of them. That statement goes to the red team before it is posted, and the desk step's sketch now says only what a found circuit would show.",
